MGAVIDEO FUN_0000_0a02 (default-palette build): restore ES/DS bases + the persistent DI across 0a50.

asm 0xa02..0xa4f: builds the 256*3 = 0x300-byte default VGA palette into the buffer segment
word[DGROUP:0x782] from the template segment word[DGROUP:0x70a].  Ghidra dropped the string-op
segment bases (dest ES=word[0x782] from DI=0, src DS=word[0x70a] at SI=0x420) AND folded the DI
register that persists across the seven FUN_0000_0a50 ramp calls (each stos-writes 0x60 bytes and
advances DI) into a single unadvanced pointer.  Reconstruct: (1) rep-movs 0x18 words template:0x420
-> buffer:0x00; (2) lodsb/shr1/stosb 0x30 bytes template:0x420 -> buffer:0x30; (3) 7x 0a50 building
32-entry 3-byte ramps from buffer:0x60, advancing the buffer pointer 0x60 per call (0x60 + 7*0x60 =
0x300).  FUN_0000_0a50 is faithful once given an absolute g_mem pointer (its int*-word/byte stride is
already correct).  Asm-verified MGAVIDEO 0x0a02.
